A||N||13||fierose||Is there any damage from removing a/c belt?||||1||
Z||000000||fierose||03-16-2001||02:49 PM||||Just wondering if there is anything that can be damage from running the car without the a/c.  A/C not exactly working right now and figured why not get the extra mile per gallon.  Not to mention it's squeeling because after it "broke in" I haven't had time to tighten it up.  Any help from experience would be greatly appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||03-16-2001||03:22 PM||||I hope not. My AC compressor defecated itself last summer. Sice running the defrost involves the AC clutch locking for some reason, I was unable to use my defrost without sending a plume of burnt belt smoke out. After having my windsheild completely ice up on the freeway in an sleet storm, I got out the handy swiss army and cut the belt off. No problems to report.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierose||03-16-2001||03:26 PM||||Thanks Stimpy.  I was pretty sure that there wouldn't be any problems didn't want to trash a belt and then find out I would have to buy another.  The only time it squeels is when it snowing or raining.  wish there was a way to keep water out of the compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wjluciano||03-16-2001||03:30 PM||||wouldnt hurt a thing that belt only drive the ac unit nothing else||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||03-16-2001||05:00 PM||||Won't hurt anything.<P>Stimpy, the reason the AC comes on for Defrost is to help dry the air. Blowing air across a colder surface causes some of the moisture in it to condense on that surface. That's why cars drip a lot of water from underneath on a really hot humid day with the AC on. For defrost it blows across the AC coil to dry it out then the heater coil to warm it up then on to the windshield where in theoretically removes the fog on the inside a little quicker.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||03-16-2001||05:02 PM||||Good timing on that question..I just cut mine off yesterday. M7F||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||03-16-2001||06:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierose:<BR><B>Just wondering if there is anything that can be damage from running the car without the a/c.  A/C not exactly working right now and figured why not get the extra mile per gallon.  Not to mention it's squeeling because after it "broke in" I haven't had time to tighten it up.  Any help from experience would be greatly appreciated.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now that you have the belt off, get a double grove pulley for the alternator and run two belts to it!<BR>  crash...<BR>||||reg||1
