Z||000010||KRMFiero||03-17-2001||01:55 PM||||hehe When i bought the car, I was told A/C works great.. when i opened the hood when i got hme i saw there was no belt on it hehe, i hope it was just sqeeking, i'll have to pick up a belt, anyone know the size?  85 Duke||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierose||03-17-2001||01:58 PM||||I got mine at autozone.  It was a really tight fit.  Took a lot of muscle for me to get it on.  If my memory serves me you'll also have to take of the alternator belt to get to it.  There are some posts on tips to doing this.  Definitely need a good pry bar.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||03-17-2001||02:10 PM||||You won't save any significant gas mileage by loosing the AC belt. If the compressor is good leave the belt on. Otherwise the pulley will rust and chew up any new belt you put on later. The rust can be bad enough that it ruins the pulley so belts won't ever last on it.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierose||03-17-2001||02:23 PM||||Good point Ogre.  I'm just taking mine off till I have time to tighten it right and fix my AC while I'm at it.||||reg||1
